From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] Plutonium: embedded surfaces: SurfaceEmbed, input
 routing and hit testing

Pages show other surfaces (Exo windows, tabs) through SurfaceEmbed; input reaches them through the input router and viz's hit testing, and drags that leave them end properly.

It holds these changes:
- shell mode on DRM, evdev input fix, display-plane path
- a tab's context menu item runs with the tab focused
- a drag that ends outside an embedded window leaves it
- an app's interactive move or resize hands the drag to the page
- a tab dragged partly off the screen overflows instead of laying out again
- a tab's <embed> ignores surface ids from its last embedding

and the parts in these files of:
- Exo embedding (Phase 1) and window broker (Phase 2)
- keep windows off the desktop, wl_output v4, embed input logs
- tab automation over DevTools, SurfaceEmbed fixes
- native fullscreen for embedded apps and tabs, Super+F, shell shortcuts
- several live shells, Super+Tab switches between them
- niri shell keys, touchpad and scrolling, drag and drop, shell links as tabs
- Chrome's own UI in the shell (DevTools, context menus, keys)
- Google sign-in on the web; tabs fullscreen outside the shells
- shm buffers the GPU can't import don't stall the display; EXO-DIAG logs at VLOG(1)
- unit tests for the broker and grant checks
- several displays, a shell per display, one window in one place
- a floating native window keeps its client-side resize edges
